WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.701
-Our first guest tonight
is one of the biggest

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:03.801
movie stars in the world.

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:05.968
She's starring in the new movie
"Sing 2,"

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:08.667
which is in theaters
Wednesday, December 22nd.

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:11.534
Please welcome
Scarlett Johansson!

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:12.868
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:14.767
Yes, that's what I'm
talking about!

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.968
Come on now! Yeah!

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:18.567
Ah!

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:20.934
Scarlett,
I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:20.934 --> 00:00:22.868
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.868
-Thank you.
It's great to be here.

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:26.000
-Yeah.
-To be here.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.067
-I did get to see you
in person recently

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.667
at the Kennedy Center Honors.

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:34.033
-That's right, the Kennedy
Center Honors in D.C.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.334
That was a couple of weeks ago
now

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:40.667
and was, I think, the latest
I've been up in about,

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.434
I would say, 2 1/2 years.

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:44.968
-[ Laughs ] Is that right?
Because of the baby?

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:46.267
-Yeah.
-How is the new baby?

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:47.434
How's everything going?

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:49.133
-So far, so good.
-Yeah.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.467
How do you like having two kids
at home?

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:52.067
How does your older daughter
feel?

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:56.000
-My daughter, Rose, is 7,
so she's in second grade.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.100
-Cute.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:01.000
-She has a lot going on
in her life.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.801
She's got a very active
social calendar.

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:04.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:07.834
So she's not -- Yeah.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:12.100
She's not as interested in
the baby as --

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:16.000
-I don't know. Let's say, like,
any other thing, really.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.467
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:21.200
-Is she at the age where she's
embarrassed by you or not yet?

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.567
-Yeah, she's embarrassed by me
because I do a little dance

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.234
when the school bus pulls up.

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:28.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:30.100
And she doesn't like that.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.767
-"Don't do that, Mom, please.
Why do you have to be --" Yeah.

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:34.701
-Yeah, she doesn't like that.

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:36.667
So, of course,
and then I just do it --

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.200
I exaggerate it even further.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.000
She's at a phase right now
where she keeps telling me

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.267
that I can't tell her
what to do.

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:46.200
[ Laughter ]
Which to me, I'm like...

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.834
I'm not going to argue with her
about it.

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:48.868
-Of course not.
But you're like,

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:50.100
"Of course I can tell you
what to do."

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.667
Yeah. "You're a child.
You're a baby."

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:54.434
-That seems like a conversation
that's not going anywhere good.

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:56.267
-I want to talk to you
about "Sing 2."

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.634
You're very funny in the movie,
but I also --

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:00.400
I heard that you do
a Cher impression.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.367
Is that true?
-Yeah.

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:05.033
I do a Cher impression.
Yeah, I do. I do.

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:06.634
I haven't broken it out
in a while.

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:09.367
I don't think I've broken it out
since I got my tonsils removed.

00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:11.834
-Was it -- Is it --
"Do you believe?"

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:13.901
What's your impression?
What song do you do?

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:15.234
-[ Clears throat ]

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.634
♪ What am I suppo-- ♪
I don't know.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:19.434
[ as Cher ] ♪ Sit around
and wait for you ♪

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:21.234
♪ Well, I can't do that ♪

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:23.133
♪ No turning back ♪

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:24.534
-No way! Oh, my God!
Hey, that was it!

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:25.634
-[ Normal voice ]
That's not bad.

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:27.100
-♪ No turning back ♪

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:29.234
Oh, my God, that was a good one.

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:31.467
Do you do karaoke?

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:33.067
I guess no one --
No one really does it.

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:35.868
-I did karaoke
for my recent birthday, yeah.

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:38.367
I did karaoke
for my recent birthday.

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:43.634
I hadn't done it in so long
and -- Yeah, it was everything.

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.601
-What's your go-to song?

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:47.300
-Um...

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.033
My go-to song...

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:52.267
I mean, I like to kind of --
I like to tease the crowd.

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:55.000
So first I like to start off
with something a little bit

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.434
sort of, like, a little kind of
intimate, emotional.

00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:00.567
I'd go with, like,
a Fleetwood Mac song actually.

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:03.367
-Ooh.
-And then -- But, like,

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:05.033
one of the more -- you know,
like, maybe "Landslide"

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.033
so people are like, "Whoa!"

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.934
Kind of everybody is
in the room now.

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:10.501
[ Laughter ]
Then I like to kind of --

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:12.601
I like to ramp it up
a little bit

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:15.467
and then I'll do
a Billy Joel song

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:18.567
like when we're maybe
three tequila shots in.

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:19.834
-Yep, that's very smart.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:23.133
This is all good.
-And then after that, I like to

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:26.701
bring the group together
and everybody,

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:28.467
I like to join --
everybody join in

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:31.501
for a rendition of
"Bohemian Rhapsody."

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:33.901
-That's exactly the right way
to do it.

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:36.267
See? You're a pro.
You know exactly what's up.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:37.667
-I know.
-In the movie,

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:39.567
Ash gets to meet her hero.

00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:41.567
Was there ever a moment
in your life where you're like,

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:43.033
"I'm nervous to meet
this person,"

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:46.601
and then it turned out to be
actually awesome and relaxing?

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.133
-Yeah. I met Judge Judy once.

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:50.467
And...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:53.868
-Wow.
-I was in a restaurant

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:57.434
and I saw Judge Judy at a table
with her family.

00:03:57.434 --> 00:03:59.934
And I -- Oh, my God.
I was so star-struck.

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:02.067
I couldn't believe it.
-Yeah.

00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:04.200
Were you afraid a little bit
that she might

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.267
judge you or say something?
-Like, judge me?

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:07.567
[ Laughter ]
-Yes, of course.

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:08.901
It's what she does for a living.
Yeah.

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:10.834
I'd be afraid.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:12.734
-Yeah, I was a little nervous.

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:15.100
I didn't know if she was going
to, you know --

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.734
I mean, she's like --
she's like an icon, obviously.

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:21.601
-Yeah, of course.
-And so, I don't know.

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:23.767
I didn't know if she was going
to look at me and be like,

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:26.400
"Get away from my table.
I'm here with my family."

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.033
And, like, you know.
-"Zip it."

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.400
-"I'm Judge Judy.
Leave me alone."

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.667
-Yeah, exactly.

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:32.567
-She wasn't like that. No.

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:36.934
She was wonderful,
and I was so relieved

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:39.801
that she was a very nice person
and she probably was like --

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:45.968
Also, I think she was surprised
that I was there and I was --

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:47.801
Oh, I was very geeked out.
-Yeah.

00:04:47.801 --> 00:04:49.367
-I mean, I grew up with
Judge Judy.

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:50.901
-Me too. We all did.

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:53.000
-Yeah, she's amazing.
-She's the greatest.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.901
But she was very, very nice.

00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:57.868
-Well, once you meet her, then
you go, "Yeah, everyone else

00:04:57.868 --> 00:04:59.868
should be cake,"
and that's how you get to do --

00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:01.901
get to sing a song with Bono.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.801
You're like, "Oh, yeah. Please.
I already met Judge Judy.

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:05.868
Bono is --"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:08.334
-I would love to do a duet
with Judge Judy.

00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:10.534
[ Laughter ]
-"Sing 3."

00:05:10.534 --> 00:05:13.067
Let's make it happen.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:15.934
Can you tell everyone
what's happening in "Sing 2"?

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:18.300
-What is happening in "Sing 2"?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.400
-Well, I will tell you
what's happening in "Sing 2."

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.467
You guys are trying to go to
this giant casino.

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:27.400
You're taking the show to, like,
a giant -- basically Vegas.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.100
A version of Vegas.
-Great. And then what?

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.634
[ Laughter ]
Then what happens?

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:34.968
-Then you meet Bobby Cannavale's
character, who's Jimmy Crystal.

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:37.334
And he's like --
-I love Bobby Cannavale.

00:05:37.334 --> 00:05:38.367
-Well, he's in the movie.

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:40.133
[ Laughter ]
-Cool!

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:41.367
-Yeah, you're going to
freak out.

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:42.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:44.667
-Oh, my God! He's the best.
-But do they pull it off?

00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:45.801
Do they not pull it off?

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:47.501
I mean, it's -- it's --
-Do they?

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:49.767
-The stakes are higher.
The stakes are higher.

00:05:49.767 --> 00:05:51.033
And you have Scarlett Johansson

00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:52.868
and you have Bono,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:55.834
What more could you ask for?

00:05:55.834 --> 00:05:57.601
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:57.601 --> 00:06:01.100
Here's Scarlett Johansson
singing with Bono in "Sing 2."

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:02.334
Take a look at this.

00:06:02.334 --> 00:06:04.033
-♪ You broke the bonds ♪

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:07.033
♪ And you loosed the chains ♪

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:09.400
♪ You carried the cross ♪

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.400
♪ Of my shame ♪

00:06:11.801 --> 00:06:15.834
♪ Of my shame ♪

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:19.434
♪ You know I believe it ♪

00:06:21.367 --> 00:06:28.567
♪ But I still haven't found
what I'm looking for ♪

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:38.367
♪ But I still haven't found
what I'm looking for ♪

00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:40.300
[ Cheers and Applause ]
-I mean, how cute is that?

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.767
Hedgehog, it's so cute!

00:06:42.767 --> 00:06:44.567
Scarlett Johansson, everybody.
-Porcupine! Porcupine!

00:06:44.567 --> 00:06:47.300
-"Sing 2" is in theaters
December 22nd.

